57:44.500 --> 57:47.760
Inflation explains how those acoustic peaks synchronized.

57:48.640 --> 57:51.520
Expyrotic cosmology cannot even attempt to calculate them

57:51.520 --> 57:54.120
until it figures out how to interact with gravity.

57:54.120 --> 57:57.440
So, you have an engine that runs perfectly on a test stand,

57:57.540 --> 58:01.740
but you haven't figured out how to attach it to the wheels or the transmission of reality.

58:01.920 --> 58:02.320
Exactly.

58:03.080 --> 58:06.860
Problem number four is the horizon problem, which we mentioned at the very beginning of the show.

58:07.180 --> 58:09.340
How does expyrotic cosmology struggle here?

58:10.020 --> 58:14.980
Well, standard inflation solves the horizon problem by taking a tiny connected patch of space

58:14.980 --> 58:17.320
and stretching it infinitely fast,

58:17.740 --> 58:21.860
explaining why opposite sides of the universe have the exact same temperature.

58:21.860 --> 58:26.120
But expyrotic cosmology removes that rapid stretching.

58:26.780 --> 58:27.220
Right.

58:27.380 --> 58:28.640
And if you remove the stretching,

58:29.060 --> 58:31.780
you still have to explain how region A and region B,

58:32.180 --> 58:33.540
separated by billions of light years,

58:33.680 --> 58:35.480
possess the same memory and temperature.

58:36.300 --> 58:41.380
The model desperately needs an explicitly causal, finite duration map

58:41.380 --> 58:44.540
to explain how this memory system connects distant regions

58:44.540 --> 58:46.460
without violating the speed of light.

58:46.580 --> 58:49.040
Right now, that map does not exist.

58:49.040 --> 58:53.680
Problem number five is the physical meaning of the auxiliary density S.

58:54.200 --> 58:56.100
We leaned heavily on the IT analogy,

58:56.380 --> 58:58.380
mutual information and conditional entropy.

58:59.060 --> 59:02.920
But Flyxion explicitly admits that the information theoretic interpretation

59:02.920 --> 59:05.060
is just a closure hypothesis,

59:05.340 --> 59:07.200
a way to make the math logically coherent.

59:07.460 --> 59:08.920
What is S physically made of?

59:09.380 --> 59:10.800
Is it a new quantum particle?

59:11.240 --> 59:12.920
A byproduct of dark energy?

59:12.920 --> 59:16.580
The paper remains entirely silent on its physical origin.

59:17.220 --> 59:20.300
Problem number six questions the very nature of the epoch structure.

59:20.900 --> 59:24.140
We discussed the requirement for 100 million to a billion cycles

59:24.140 --> 59:26.140
to match the infrared suppression data.

59:26.400 --> 59:27.640
But what are these cycles?

59:28.400 --> 59:31.360
Are they actual chronological phases in time?

59:31.860 --> 59:35.140
Did the universe physically reset a billion times?

59:35.140 --> 59:39.400
Or are these epochs merely mathematical bookkeeping devices

59:39.400 --> 59:43.800
representing a single, continuous, ongoing, fluid process?

59:43.800 --> 59:47.080
The physics community will have to decide how to interpret the math.

59:47.480 --> 59:47.700
Yes.

59:48.260 --> 59:52.160
Problem number seven involves the boundedness of the free energy below.

59:52.980 --> 59:55.220
We established in Proposition 5.2

59:55.220 --> 59:58.200
that the free energy smoothly dissipates and decreases.

59:58.780 --> 01:00:00.840
But does it have a hard floor?

01:00:01.420 --> 01:00:03.740
Does the energy stop at a baseline of zero?

01:00:03.740 --> 01:00:06.700
Or can the math allow it to fall infinitely

01:00:06.700 --> 01:00:09.720
into negative energy states, destroying the universe?

01:00:10.580 --> 01:00:12.480
The equations aren't locked down tightly enough yet

01:00:12.480 --> 01:00:13.780
to prevent infinite collapse.

01:00:14.340 --> 01:00:15.640
And finally, problem eight.

01:00:16.180 --> 01:00:17.520
The covariant formulation.

01:00:18.280 --> 01:00:20.440
This is intimately tied to the gravity problem.

01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:24.040
In modern physics, any valid theory must be written in a way

01:00:24.040 --> 01:00:26.460
that respects Einstein's theory of general relativity.

01:00:26.720 --> 01:00:30.340
It requires a proper, mathematically sound stress-energy tensor.

01:00:30.640 --> 01:00:33.420
And it must account for gravitational back reaction.

01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:36.920
Meaning, as the fields move, they must bend space.

01:00:37.280 --> 01:00:40.620
And that bent space must, in turn, alter how the fields move.

01:00:41.560 --> 01:00:43.860
Formulating this memory mechanism covariantly

01:00:43.860 --> 01:00:46.960
is a monumental task that remains unsolved.

01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:50.480
Eight massive gaping holes in the theory.

01:00:51.200 --> 01:00:54.320
But I appreciate the extreme intellectual honesty of the author.

01:00:54.580 --> 01:00:56.600
They didn't just claim to have solved the universe.

01:00:56.600 --> 01:00:59.940
They built an incredibly precise engine, put it on the table,

01:01:00.040 --> 01:01:02.500
and said, here are the eight pieces missing

01:01:02.500 --> 01:01:03.900
before we can put this in a car.

01:01:04.400 --> 01:01:08.240
It is a textbook example of how true collaborative science

01:01:08.240 --> 01:01:09.420
should be conducted.

01:01:10.080 --> 01:01:11.500
You build the scaffolding.

01:01:11.860 --> 01:01:14.900
You relentlessly stress test the steel beams.

01:01:15.140 --> 01:01:18.800
And you are rigorously honest about exactly where the roof is missing.

01:01:18.800 --> 01:01:24.580
We have covered an immense, staggering amount of intellectual ground today.

01:01:24.960 --> 01:01:27.140
We have traversed the history of standard inflation

01:01:27.140 --> 01:01:28.700
and its mathematical baggage.

01:01:29.340 --> 01:01:31.900
We've waded into the deep, auto-regressive,

01:01:32.160 --> 01:01:34.480
memory-relaxing waters of expyrotic cosmology.

01:01:34.800 --> 01:01:38.240
We've explored L2 flows, Wasserstein optimal transport,

01:01:38.700 --> 01:01:41.300
Poincaré recurrences, magic exponents,

01:01:41.300 --> 01:01:45.900
and the dizzying concept of a billion-cycle cosmic loop.

01:01:46.700 --> 01:01:49.860
It is an incredible amount of heavy physics to process.

01:01:50.180 --> 01:01:51.740
But as we wrap up this deep dive,

01:01:51.940 --> 01:01:53.840
I want to address you directly, the listener.

01:01:54.520 --> 01:01:56.320
Even though this model is incomplete,

01:01:56.700 --> 01:01:59.620
think about the profound shift in perspective it offers.

01:01:59.860 --> 01:02:01.160
It really does reframe everything.

01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:04.040
We are so deeply conditioned by standard science

01:02:04.040 --> 01:02:06.480
to view the universe as a ballistic projectile,

01:02:06.940 --> 01:02:10.360
a chaotic cannonball fired from a primordial Big Bang.

01:02:10.360 --> 01:02:15.340
But expyrotic cosmology asks us to imagine something far more elegant.

01:02:16.060 --> 01:02:18.900
It asks us to view the cosmos as a living document,

01:02:19.440 --> 01:02:22.280
a dynamic system that is constantly reading its own margins,

01:02:22.860 --> 01:02:24.520
checking its own deep backup files,

01:02:24.800 --> 01:02:26.800
deliberately correcting its own structural errors,

01:02:26.940 --> 01:02:30.420
and slowly, organically settling into a majestic state

01:02:30.420 --> 01:02:33.740
dictated not by the chaos of a violent explosion,

01:02:34.140 --> 01:02:36.920
but by the deep, enduring memory of its own past.

01:02:36.920 --> 01:02:40.420
And if we dare to take that information-theoretic view seriously,

01:02:40.980 --> 01:02:44.460
if the vast, intricate structure of our local galaxy

01:02:44.460 --> 01:02:46.800
is just the mathematical fixed point

01:02:46.800 --> 01:02:49.740
of the billion-cycle recursion of cosmic memory,

01:02:50.200 --> 01:02:54.640
it leaves us confronting perhaps the most profound question in existence.

01:02:54.780 --> 01:02:55.300
What's that?

01:02:55.300 --> 01:02:58.820
If the universe is actively remembering a backup file,

01:02:59.440 --> 01:03:02.780
where did the very first seed of information come from?

01:03:03.440 --> 01:03:07.640
Who, or what physical process, wrote the original code?

01:03:08.020 --> 01:03:12.200
A question that might just take another 13.8 billion years to answer.

01:03:12.760 --> 01:03:16.200
Thank you for joining us on this deep dive into the RSVP plenum

01:03:16.200 --> 01:03:17.840
and the hidden memory of the cosmos.

01:03:18.560 --> 01:03:21.240
Keep questioning the fundamental nature of everything around you,

01:03:21.520 --> 01:03:22.540
and we'll see you next time.

